{'symbol': 'ABMD', 'date': '2020-04-30 10:30:00', 'title': 'Abiomed Announces Q4 FY 2020 Revenue Of $207 Million And 28.1% Operating Margin', 'text': 'ABIOMED ANNOUNCES Q4 FY 2020 REVENUE OF $207 MILLION AND 28.1% OPERATING MARGIN.Q4 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.70.Q4 REVENUE $207 MILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $207.2 MILLION.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.94 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.WILL NOT BE PROVIDING FULL YEAR 2021 REVENUE OR OPERATING MARGIN GUIDANCE AT THIS TIME.WILL ANALYZE AND MONITOR THIS DYNAMIC ENVIRONMENT AND WILL PROVIDE AN UPDATE ON GUIDANCE WHEN APPROPRIATE.COMPANY IS TAKING PROACTIVE ACTIONS TO MITIGATE BUSINESS IMPACT OF COVID-19 TO BETTER MATCH EXPENSES TO REVENUE IN Q1.HOLD ON HIRING, ELIMINATING NON-CRITICAL CONSULTANTS, CONTRACTORS, AND TEMPORARY WORKERS.REDUCING DISCRETIONARY SPENDING AND IMPLEMENTING ALTERNATE WORK SCHEDULES FOR AACHEN AND DANVERS PRODUCTION TEAMS.CEO AND COO HAVE REDUCED THEIR SALARIES BY 100%, VPS AND DIRECTORS HAVE REDUCED THEIR SALARIES BY 50% AND 20% RESPECTIVELY FOR Q1.BOARD OF DIRECTORS HAVE ALSO REDUCED THEIR CASH RETAINERS BY 50% FOR Q1.NON-DIRECTOR EMPLOYEES AT MASSACHUSETTS AND GERMAN HEADQUARTERS WILL BE TAKING A MINIMUM OF ONE-WEEK FURLOUGH OR UNUSED VACATION.FIELD TEAM WILL WORK ON MONTHLY OPERATING PLANS TO ALLOW FOR FLEXIBILITY AND POTENTIAL TO INCREASE SEQUENTIALLY EACH WEEK.'}
{'symbol': 'AFL', 'date': '2020-04-30 19:30:00', 'title': 'Aflac Incorporated Announces First Quarter Results', 'text': 'ORPORATED ANNOUNCES FIRST QUARTER RESULTS, REPORTS FIRST QUARTER NET EARNINGS OF $566 MILLION, WITHDRAWS ANNUAL ADJUSTED EPS GUIDANCE, DECLARES SECOND QUARTER CASH DIVIDEND.Q1 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.21.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.78.Q1 REVENUE $5.2 BILLION VERSUS $5.7 BILLION.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.10 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SALES PRODUCTION IN BOTH JAPAN AND U.S. DID BEGIN TO FALL OFF IN MARCH, AND DECLINE ACCELERATED IN MONTH OF APRIL.AFLAC U.S. NET PREMIUM INCOME ROSE 1.5% TO $1.5 BILLION IN Q1.AFLAC - WILL CONTINUE TO INVEST IN PLATFORM & GROWTH INVESTMENTS.'}
{'symbol': 'AAL', 'date': '2020-04-30 14:30:00', 'title': 'American Airlines Q1 Loss Per Share $5.26', 'text': "AMERICAN AIRLINES - QTRLY TOTAL MAINLINE & REGIONAL REVENUE PASSENGER MILES 45.17 BILLION, DOWN 17.6%.AMERICAN AIRLINES - Q1 NET LOSS OF $5.26 PER SHARE .AMERICAN AIRLINES GROUP REPORTS FIRST-QUARTER 2020 FINANCIAL RESULTS.Q1 LOSS PER SHARE $5.26.Q1 LOSS PER SHARE $2.65 EXCLUDING ITEMS.AMERICAN AIRLINES - ENDED Q1 WITH $6.8 BILLION OF AVAILABLE LIQUIDITY AND EXPECTS TO END Q2 WITH APPROXIMATELY $11 BILLION OF LIQUIDITY.AMERICAN AIRLINES - OBTAINED RIGHT TO ACCESS $10.6 BILLION IN FINANCIAL ASSISTANCE THROUGH CARES ACT.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $-2.33 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.AMERICAN AIRLINES - TEMPORARILY RELAXED ITS SEATING POLICIES AND ADJUSTED AIRPORT PROCEDURES TO ENCOURAGE SOCIAL DISTANCING.AMERICAN AIRLINES - REDUCED ONBOARD FOOD AND BEVERAGE SERVICE TO LIMIT CONTACT.AMERICAN AIRLINES - EXTENDED WAIVERS FOR TRAVEL OCCURRING THROUGH END OF SEPTEMBER 2020.AMERICAN AIRLINES - AMERICAN'S AVERAGE ESTIMATED SECOND-QUARTER 2020 CASH BURN RATE IS EXPECTED TO BE APPROXIMATELY $70 MILLION PER DAY.AMERICAN AIRLINES - IN Q1 OF 2020, COMPANY RECOGNIZED $1.4 BILLION IN NET SPECIAL ITEMS BEFORE EFFECT OF INCOME TAXES.AMERICAN AIRLINES - EXPECTS TO PLEDGE PORTION OF ASSETS AS COLLATERAL FOR FUTURE FINANCINGS, INCLUDING ABOUT $4.75 BILLION SECURED LOAN CO HAS APPLIED FOR UNDER CARES ACT.AMERICAN AIRLINES - ESTIMATES REDUCTION OF MORE THAN $12 BILLION IN ITS 2020 OPERATING AND CAPITAL EXPENDITURES."}
