{'symbol': 'MSFT', 'date': '2020-04-30 18:30:00', 'title': 'Microsoft Q3 Earnings Per Share Of $1.40', 'text': 'QUARTERLY DILUTED EARNINGS PER SHARE WAS $1.40.QUARTERLY REVENUE WAS $35.0 BILLION AND INCREASED 15%.MICROSOFT - COVID-19 HAD MINIMAL NET IMPACT ON TOTAL COMPANY REVENUE IN QUARTER.QUARTERLY REVENUE IN PRODUCTIVITY AND BUSINESS PROCESSES WAS $11.7 BILLION AND INCREASED 15%.SAYS IN FINAL WEEKS OF QUARTER, THERE WAS A SLOWDOWN IN TRANSACTIONAL LICENSING, PARTICULARLY IN SMALL AND MEDIUM BUSINESSES.QUARTERLY OFFICE COMMERCIAL PRODUCTS AND CLOUD SERVICES REVENUE INCREASED 13%.SAYS IN FINAL WEEKS OF QUARTER THERE WAS A REDUCTION IN ADVERTISING SPEND IN LINKEDIN..SAYS IN PRODUCTIVITY AND BUSINESS PROCESSES AND INTELLIGENT CLOUD SEGMENTS, CLOUD USAGE INCREASED IN QUARTER.QUARTERLY LINKEDIN REVENUE INCREASED 21%.SAYS IN MORE PERSONAL COMPUTING SEGMENT, WINDOWS OEM, SURFACE BENEFITED FROM INCREASED DEMAND TO SUPPORT REMOTE WORK AND LEARN SCENARIOS IN QUARTER.SAYS IN MORE PERSONAL COMPUTING SEGMENT,WINDOWS OEM & SURFACE WAS OFFSET IN PART BY SUPPLY CHAIN CONSTRAINTS IN CHINA THAT IMPROVED LATE IN QUARTER.SAYS SEARCH WAS NEGATIVELY IMPACTED BY REDUCTIONS IN ADVERTISING SPEND, PARTICULARLY IN INDUSTRIES MOST IMPACTED BY COVID-19 IN QUARTER.SAYS EFFECTS OF COVID-19 MAY NOT BE FULLY REFLECTED IN FINANCIAL RESULTS UNTIL FUTURE PERIODS..'}
