{'symbol': 'LUV', 'date': '2020-04-30 19:30:00', 'title': 'Southwest Airlines Announces Pricing Of Notes', 'text': 'SOUTHWEST AIRLINES ANNOUNCES PRICING OF NOTES.SOUTHWEST AIRLINES CO - PRICED ITS UNDERWRITTEN PUBLIC OFFERING OF $2.0 BILLION OF SENIOR NOTES.SOUTHWEST AIRLINES CO - PRICED $2.0 BILLION SENIOR NOTES, CONSISTING OF $750 MILLION OF 4.750% NOTES DUE 2023 AND $1.25 BILLION OF 5.250% NOTES DUE 2025.SOUTHWEST AIRLINES CO - 2023 NOTES WILL BE ISSUED AT 99.586% OF PAR AND 2025 NOTES WILL BE ISSUED AT 99.783% OF PAR.SOUTHWEST AIRLINES - TO USE NET PROCEEDS FROM OFFERING TO REPAY A PORTION OF OUTSTANDING BORROWINGS UNDER AMENDED & RESTATED 364-DAY CREDIT AGREEMENT.'}
{'symbol': 'TPR', 'date': '2020-04-30 09:30:00', 'title': 'Tapestry Q3 Diluted EPS Loss 2.45 USD', 'text': "Q3 DILUTED EPS LOSS 2.45 USD.NET SALES TOTALED $1.07 BILLION FOR FISCAL Q3 AS COMPARED TO $1.33 BILLION IN PRIOR YEAR.NOT PROVIDING GUIDANCE FOR ITS FISCAL Q4 AND FULL YEAR 2020.IN Q3 OF FISCAL 2020, COMPANY RECORDED $267 MILLION OF IMPAIRMENT CHARGES TO INDEFINITE-LIVED BRAND INTANGIBLE ASSETS.IN Q3 OF FISCAL 2020, COMPANY RECORDED $211 MILLION OF IMPAIRMENT CHARGES TO GOODWILL FOR STUART WEITZMAN REPORTING UNIT.NET SALES FOR COACH TOTALED APPROXIMATELY $772 MILLION FOR FISCAL Q3 AS COMPARED TO $965 MILLION IN PRIOR YEAR.NET SALES FOR KATE SPADE TOTALED APPROXIMATELY $250 MILLION FOR FISCAL Q3 AS COMPARED TO $281 MILLION IN PRIOR YEAR.NOT PROVIDING COMPARABLE STORE SALES FIGURES.TAKING ADDITIONAL ACTIONS TO FURTHER STREAMLINE ITS ORGANIZATION, INCLUDING REDUCTIONS IN ITS CORPORATE AND RETAIL WORKFORCE.TAPESTRY - EXPECTS TO INCUR PRE-TAX CHARGES ASSOCIATED WITH COST ACTIONS OF ABOUT $55-$70 MILLION WHICH WILL BE REFLECTED BEGINNING IN Q4.TAPESTRY'S SUPPLY CHAIN CONTINUED TO OPERATE EFFECTIVELY OVER Q3.AS OF MID-APRIL ALL CHINA STORES WERE OPEN AND WE HAVE CONTINUED TO EXPERIENCE A GRADUAL IMPROVEMENT IN BUSINESS WEEK-TO-WEEK.QTRLY  ADJUSTED LOSS PER SHARE $0.27.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $-0.12, REVENUE VIEW $1.03 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA."}
{'symbol': 'TFX', 'date': '2020-04-30 15:30:00', 'title': 'FDA Says Vascular Solutions Recalls Langston Dual Lumen Catheter Due To Risk Of Separation During Use', 'text': 'FDA SAYS VASCULAR SOLUTIONS RECALLS LANGSTON DUAL LUMEN CATHETER DUE TO RISK OF SEPARATION DURING USE.FDA SAYS VASCULAR SOLUTIONS RECALLED 4,304  LANGSTON DUAL LUMEN CATHETER DEVICES IN THE U.S..FDA SAYS THERE HAVE BEEN 8 COMPLAINTS AND NO REPORTS OF INJURY OR DEATH RELATED TO VASCULAR SOLUTIONS LANGSTON DUAL LUMEN CATHETER.FDA SAYS IT IDENTIFIED VASCULAR SOLUTIONS LANGSTON DUAL LUMEN CATHETER RECALL AS A CLASS I RECALL.'}
{'symbol': 'TFX', 'date': '2020-04-30 09:30:00', 'title': 'Teleflex Reports First Quarter 2020 Results', 'text': 'TELEFLEX REPORTS FIRST QUARTER 2020 RESULTS.Q1 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.72 FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS.Q1 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.78 FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS.Q1 REVENUE $630.6 MILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $620.6 MILLION.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $2.35 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.WITHDRAWS PREVIOUSLY PROVIDED 2020 FINANCIAL GUIDANCE DUE TO COVID-19 PANDEMIC.REMAINS IN A STRONG FINANCIAL POSITION, SUPPORTED BY A HEALTHY BALANCE SHEET, WHICH INCLUDES OVER $400 MILLION OF CASH ON HAND.CANNOT ACCURATELY PREDICT SPECIFIC EXTENT OR DURATION OF IMPACT OF COVID-19 OUTBREAK ON ITS FINANCIAL AND OPERATING RESULTS.DURING Q1 SAW A NEGATIVE IMPACT FROM COVID-19 IN AMERICAS AND ASIA.DURING Q1 EMEA SAW A BENEFIT DUE TO ELEVATED ORDERING FOR CERTAIN ANESTHESIA, RESPIRATORY, AND VASCULAR ACCESS PRODUCTS.ANTICIPATES MATERIAL DISRUPTION CAUSED BY EVOLVING COVID-19 PANDEMIC AND MACROECONOMIC ENVIRONMENT.WILL NOT UPDATE 2020 GUIDANCE UNTIL IMPACT OF COVID-19 BECOMES SUFFICIENTLY CLEAR.'}
{'symbol': 'TSLA', 'date': '2020-04-30 18:30:00', 'title': 'Tesla Says Q1 EPS Attributable To Common Stockholders, Basic (Non-GAAP) Of $1.24', 'text': 'TESLA INC -  QTRLY EPS ATTRIBUTABLE TO COMMON STOCKHOLDERS, BASIC (NON-GAAP) $1.24.TESLA INC - OPERATING CASH FLOW LESS CAPEX (FREE CASH FLOW) NEGATIVE $895M IN Q1 (OF WHICH $981M OUTFLOW DUE TO INVENTORY GROWTH).TESLA INC - Q1 2020 WAS THE FIRST TIME IN OUR HISTORY THAT WE ACHIEVED A POSITIVE GAAP NET INCOME IN THE SEASONALLY WEAK FIRST QUARTER.TESLA INC - QUARTER-END CASH AND CASH EQUIVALENTS INCREASED BY $1.8 BILLION QOQ TO $8.1 BILLION.TESLA SAYS  DESPITE GLOBAL OPERATIONAL CHALLENGES, WE WERE ABLE TO ACHIEVE OUR \'BEST FIRST QUARTER FOR BOTH PRODUCTION AND DELIVERIES\'.TESLA INC -  MODEL Y CONTRIBUTED PROFITS, WHICH IS THE FIRST TIME IN OUR HISTORY THAT A NEW PRODUCT HAS BEEN PROFITABLE IN ITS FIRST QUARTER.TESLA INC - IN QUARTER, CAPITAL EXPENDITURES INCREASED SEQUENTIALLY MAINLY DUE TO INVESTMENTS IN MODEL Y PREPARATIONS IN FREMONT & GIGAFACTORY SHANGHAI.TESLA SAYS REMAIN CONFIDENT IN GROWING GLOBAL PRODUCTION CAPACITY AS "QUICKLY AS POSSIBLE".TESLA INC -  ARE ON TRACK TO START THE FIRST MODEL Y DELIVERIES FROM GIGAFACTORY BERLIN IN 2021.TESLA INC - CONTINUING TO INVEST IN PRODUCT ROADMAP, INCLUDING IMPROVEMENTS IN TECHNOLOGY, AS WELL AS LOCALIZING PRODUCTION IN SHANGHAI & BERLIN.TESLA SAYS BELIEVE WE ARE WELL-POSITIONED TO MANAGE NEAR-TERM UNCERTAINTY WHILE ACHIEVING OUR LONG-TERM PLANS.TESLA SAYS  NEAR-TERM PROFIT GUIDANCE IS CURRENTLY ON HOLD.'}
{'symbol': 'TXT', 'date': '2020-04-30 11:30:00', 'title': 'Textron CEO Says Customer NetJets Canceled Some Orders - Conf Call', 'text': 'TEXTRON SAYS HAD SEVERAL JET DELIVERIES PUSH OUT OF Q1 DUE TO COVID-19 - CONF CALL.TEXTRON EXPECTS AIRCRAFT WILL DELIVER AS TRAVEL RESTRICTIONS BEGIN TO EASE.TEXTRON SAYS EXPECTS LOWER JET DELIVERIES IN Q2.TEXTRON CFO SAYS HAS SUSPENDED SHARE REPURCHASES - CONF CALL.TEXTRON CFO SAYS HAS SUFFICIENT LIQUIDITY TO FUND OPERATIONS.TEXTRON CEO SAYS EXPECTS EUROPE AND AMERICA TO RESUME AUTOMOTIVE PRODUCTION IN Q2.TEXTRON CEO SAYS HAS SUSPENDED MOST PRODUCTION IN AVIATION UNIT THROUGH END OF MAY.TEXTRON CEO SAYS DO NOT VIEW THE PRE-OWNED JET MARKET AS AN IMPEDIMENT FOR SALE OF NEW AIRCRAFT.TEXTRON CEO SAYS POSSIBLE AIRCRAFT DEMAND DESTRUCTION FROM COVID-19 IS A BIG UNKNOWN.TEXTRON CFO SAYS EXPECTS TO BE CASH POSITIVE IN THE BACK END OF THE YEAR.TEXTRON CEO SAYS CUSTOMER NETJETS CANCELED SOME ORDERS.'}
{'symbol': 'TWTR', 'date': '2020-04-30 12:30:00', 'title': 'Twitter Reports Qtrly Adjusted Net Loss Per Share $0.01', 'text': 'TWITTER INC - QTRLY NET LOSS PER SHARE $0.01; QTRLY REVENUE $807.64 MILLION VERSUS $786.89 MILLION.TWITTER INC - QTRLY AVERAGE MONETIZABLE DAILY ACTIVE USERS WERE 166 MILLION VERSUS 134 MILLION.TWITTER INC -  QTRLY NON-GAAP NET INCOME PER SHARE $0.11; QTRLY ADJUSTED NET LOSS PER SHARE $0.01.TWITTER INC - QTRLY COSTS & EXPENSES $815 MILLION, AN INCREASE OF 18%.TWITTER INC - QTRLY ADVERTISING REVENUE $682 MILLION, UP ABOUT $3 MILLION.TWITTER INC - QTRLY AVERAGE U.S. MDAU 33 MILLION VERSUS 28 MILLION; QTRLY AVERAGE INTERNATIONAL MDAU 133 MILLION VERSUS 105 MILLION.TWITTER INC - SAW STRONG MDAU GROWTH THROUGHOUT THE QUARTER, WITH AN ACCELERATION IN MARCH AS THE PANDEMIC BECAME GLOBAL.TWITTER INC - REDUCED COMPANY HIRING AND NON-LABOR EXPENSE PLANS TO LOWER EXPENSE GROWTH.TWITTER INC - FROM MARCH 11 UNTIL MARCH 31, TOTAL ADVERTISING REVENUE DECLINED ABOUT 27%.TWITTER INC - AVERAGE MDAU GREW 24% IN QUARTER, DRIVEN BY SEASONAL STRENGTH, CONVERSATION RELATED TO COVID-19 PANDEMIC.TWITTER INC - QTRLY AD ENGAGEMENTS UP 25%, RESULTING FROM INCREASED IMPRESSIONS DRIVEN BY AUDIENCE GROWTH & IMPROVED CLICKTHROUGH RATES.TWITTER INC - QTRLY COST PER ENGAGEMENT FELL 19%, DRIVEN BY LIKE-FOR-LIKE PRICE DECREASES ACROSS MOST AD FORMATS & LOWER DEMAND IN MARCH.TWITTER INC -  AD REVENUE DOWNTURN IN MARCH WAS PARTICULARLY PRONOUNCED IN U.S., AND AD WEAKNESS IN ASIA BEGAN TO SUBSIDE AS RESTRICTIONS WERE GRADUALLY LIFTED.'}
{'symbol': 'TYL', 'date': '2020-04-30 19:30:00', 'title': 'Tyler Technologies Reports Earnings For First Quarter 2020', 'text': 'TYLER TECHNOLOGIES REPORTS EARNINGS FOR FIRST QUARTER 2020.Q1 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.25.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.16.Q1 REVENUE $276.8 MILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $280 MILLION.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.25 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.AT QUARTER END, TOTAL BACKLOG WAS $1.50 BILLION, UP 19.2% FROM $1.26 BILLION AT MARCH 31, 2019.ESTIMATE THAT Q1 REVENUES WERE REDUCED BY APPROXIMATELY $6 MILLION AS A RESULT OF COVID-19.TYLER TECHNOLOGIES - EXPECT RECURRING REVENUES, WHICH COMPRISE ABOUT 70% OF OUR TOTAL REVENUES, WILL NOT BE SIGNIFICANTLY AFFECTED BY COVID-19.ANTICIPATE A GREATER IMPACT FROM COVID-19 IN SECOND AND THIRD QUARTERS.DO NOT EXPECT TO ELIMINATE ANY POSITIONS, BUT ANTICIPATE INCREMENTAL HIRING WILL BE REDUCED SOMEWHAT FROM ORIGINAL PLANS.CONFIDENT IN OUR LONG-TERM OUTLOOK.'}
